 "MY-H861": {
  "lawId": "MY-H861",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These Regulations may be cited as the Malaysian Quarantine and\nInspection Services (Registration of Importers, Exporters or Agents) Regulations\n (2) These Regulations come into operation on 1 April 2013.\nRegistration of importers, exporters and agents"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. Any person shall not import or export any plant, animal, carcass, fish, agricultural\nproduce, soil or microorganism unless that person is registered with the Director\nGeneral as an importer, exporter or agent.\n\n Application and approval of registration"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1)  An applicant shall make an application for registration  as an importer,\nexporter or agent of  plant, animal , carcass, fish, agricultural produce , soil or\nmicroorganism to the Director General  according to any manner  as determined by the\nDirector General.\n\n(2) The Director General may, upon receiving an application of registration,\nrequires the applicant to submit any  other information or documents as he  may think\nnecessary in approving the application for registration.\n\n(3) The Director General may  give his approval in writing  to any  applicant\nwho meets the conditions of registration.\n\n(4) Notwithstanding subregulation (1), any person who has registered as an\nimporter, exporter or agent with the relevant agency or department shall be deemed to\nhave been registered as an importer, exporter or agent under these Regulations.\n\nChanges in registration information"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The importer, exporter  or agent  shall notify  the Director Genera l in writing\nregarding any changes made to the registration information of the importer, exporter or\nagent within thirty days from such changes.\n\nTermination of registration"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. (1)  The Director General  may, at  any time,  terminate any  registration if the\nimporter, exporter or agent contravenes any provision of  these Regulations or any\nconditions of the registration.\n\n(2) Any importers, exporters or agents whose registration is revoked shall not\nbe entitled to any compensation for any loss suffered by him  due to the cancellation of\nregistration under these Regulations.\n\nGeneral penalty"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6. Any person who contravenes any provision under these Regulations commits an\noffence and shall, upon conviction, be liable to a fine  not exceeding one thousand ringgit\nor to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.\n\nMade 28 March 2013\n[KP/LA/483/12/1; PN(PU2)714]\n\n               DATUK SERI NOH BIN HAJI OMAR\n               Minister of Agriculture and Agro-Based Industry"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
